747
00:36:09,099 --> 00:36:11,004
“非常好，请坐下，然后把衣服全脱光？”
"Very good if you'd just like to sit, pull all your clothes off?"

748
00:36:11,038 --> 00:36:12,489
于是我就……把衣服全脱了，
So I... I took them all off,

749
00:36:12,684 --> 00:36:14,555
然后他就开始问诊。我就坐那儿……
and then he interviewed me. I sat...

750
00:36:17,054 --> 00:36:19,720
像个初生婴儿一样赤条条地坐着，
I sat naked as a baby

751
00:36:19,729 --> 00:36:23,149
在一间……非常昂贵的大诊室里，
就这样光溜溜面对着他，
in front of him like this in a... in a very
expensive big consultation room

752
00:36:23,149 --> 00:36:25,981
他一边记录我的情况，还时不时打量我，
把所有东西都记下来。
while he wrote down things about me, kept
looking at me and writing all the things down.

753
00:36:26,328 --> 00:36:29,591
接着他说：“好了，我们现在要
呃……快速做个呃……前列腺检查。”
And then he said "Right, we're just going to
uh... do a quick uh... prostate examination."

754
00:36:30,234 --> 00:36:31,006
让我弯下腰，
Bent me over,

755
00:36:31,523 --> 00:36:34,173
我向上帝发誓，他把整个头都伸进我屁股里了，
and I swear to God, stuck his head up my bottom,

756
00:36:35,980 --> 00:36:39,282
因为当他问“疼不疼？”的时候，
because when he said "Does that hurt?"

757
00:36:39,290 --> 00:36:41,373
声音是发闷的，听起来是“疼……不……疼？”
it was muffled, it was "Does that hurt?"

758
00:36:43,960 --> 00:36:45,916
那真是我这辈子经历过最剧烈的痛了。
And it was the worst pain I've ever had in my life.

759
00:36:46,255 --> 00:36:49,404
行了听着，显然，我现在非常想看看你的单圈成绩。
Ok listen, I really want to get onto your lap, obviously.

760
00:36:49,700 --> 00:36:50,801
- 好。
- 在赛道上跑得怎么样？
- Yes.
- How did it go out there?

761
00:36:51,469 --> 00:36:53,131
我觉得跑得挺烂的，呃……
I thought quite badly, um...

762
00:36:53,698 --> 00:36:56,137
我挺喜欢斯提格的，他人特别好
I like the Stig very much, he was very kind to me

763
00:36:56,306 --> 00:37:00,183
呃……但是，真不容易，这真挺难的，杰里米。
um... but uh... it's not easy, it's not easy Jeremy.

764
00:37:00,217 --> 00:37:01,825
- 你觉得难开？
- 对，真难。
- You don't think so.
- No, I don't.

765
00:37:01,825 --> 00:37:03,561
因为这完全反直觉，
'cause it's so counter-intuitive,

766
00:37:03,654 --> 00:37:04,756
懂吧？就在你心里想着：
you know? Just when you're thinking:

767
00:37:04,756 --> 00:37:06,804
“完了我要没命了，赶紧踩刹车”的时候，
Well now I'm going to die so I'll brake

768
00:37:06,829 --> 00:37:08,827
他却冲你喊：“油门踩到底！”
but he says "Flat down with the accelerator!"

769
00:37:09,114 --> 00:37:11,254
然后呃……反过来也一样，而且……
And uh... and the other way around and um...

770
00:37:11,254 --> 00:37:13,109
我……我知道我肯定成绩很烂。
I... I know I'm gonna be bad.

771
00:37:13,209 --> 00:37:15,823
现场有谁想看看休跑的那一圈吗？
Who here would like to see Hugh's lap?

772
00:37:16,102 --> 00:37:19,126
（观众）想！
- 来放录像，走着。
(Crowd) Yeah!
- Let's play the tape, here it goes.

773
00:37:19,710 --> 00:37:20,354
这就是你了
This is you

774
00:37:21,141 --> 00:37:22,175
发车了。
and there you go.

775
00:37:24,266 --> 00:37:25,172
真是辆“好车”啊。
What a car.

776
00:37:26,255 --> 00:37:28,294
- 那个……
- 头盔可真难看。
- That's...
- A very unattractive helmet.

777
00:37:28,743 --> 00:37:31,435
哎，别升挡啊，你个哔——！
Oh, don't change gear, you [beep]!

778
00:37:33,569 --> 00:37:35,990
- 我的老天爷啊！
- 那不可能是我跑得最好的一……
- Crikey Moses!
- That can not be my best...

779
00:37:38,708 --> 00:37:39,555
这下挺沉稳嘛。
that's quite grown up.

780
00:37:39,555 --> 00:37:41,434
那段过得相当漂亮，太棒了。
That was very good through there, excellent.

781
00:37:41,435 --> 00:37:43,165
- 哎不过你现在这是往哪儿开呢？是啊。
- 那是……
- Oh where are you going now though? Yeah.
- That's...

782
00:37:44,245 --> 00:37:45,379
锤头弯
Hammerhead

783
00:37:45,794 --> 00:37:48,071
- 看着又顺又快
- 我就从来没玩明白过锤头弯
- looking smooth and fast
- I never mastered the Hammerhead

784
00:37:48,579 --> 00:37:50,137
- 那下算违规罚时吗？
- 走得挺好，没罚，很棒。
- Is that a penalty?
- That's good, no that's good.

785
00:37:50,857 --> 00:37:51,736
这里的走线不错。
Good line through there.

786
00:37:52,033 --> 00:37:53,836
噢，简直是一件“艺术品”
Oh that was a piece of "art"

787
00:37:54,809 --> 00:37:56,435
我哔——
Oh [beep]

788
00:37:57,053 --> 00:38:00,029
马上你就要切进内线了，到时候你肯定就不骂街了。
Soon you're gonna cut inside and you won't be swearing.

789
00:38:00,029 --> 00:38:01,147
从这儿过速度会很快吗？
Is it gonna be fast through here?

790
00:38:01,147 --> 00:38:03,069
瞧见没？每次我摇摇晃晃过弯的时候，
See? Every time I came wobbling through a turn

791
00:38:03,179 --> 00:38:05,862
正前方总会杵着另一个前BBC摄像师挡我道。
there was another ex-BBC camera man right in my way.

792
00:38:06,480 --> 00:38:08,190
又彻底搞砸了。
Did exactly the wrong thing again.

793
00:38:09,291 --> 00:38:10,645
好了，最后一个弯
And here we are, last corner

794
00:38:10,934 --> 00:38:12,306
- 这段开得奇烂无比
- 推头推出去了
- This is very poor
- That's going wide

795
00:38:12,307 --> 00:38:15,281
但是，哇，漂亮！冲线！
that's wow yes! Across the line!

796
00:38:16,331 --> 00:38:16,737
现在
Now

797
00:38:23,412 --> 00:38:24,242
我呃……
I um...

798
00:38:26,062 --> 00:38:29,118
我知道开得不怎么样，我知道，我感觉……
我感觉自己辜负了所有人……每一个人
I know it's not good, I know, I feel...
I feel like I've let anyone... everyone down

799
00:38:29,177 --> 00:38:30,733
- 连斯提格我也辜负了。
- 哪有的事，什么叫辜负大家？你顶多就对不起你自己。
- and including the Stig.
- No, what do you mean? It's only yourself.

800
00:38:32,299 --> 00:38:34,712
那你觉得自己能排在那个……圈速榜的什么位置？
So where do you think you've come on the um...

801
00:38:34,805 --> 00:38:36,156
- 在圈速榜上？
- 唉，我要是知道就好了。
- on the board?
- Ah, I wish I knew.

802
00:38:36,156 --> 00:38:38,453
我最想……反正我可不想输给……
Who would I really like... I wouldn't like to come lower

803
00:38:39,215 --> 00:38:41,255
迈克尔·甘本。
than Michael Gambon.

804
00:38:41,416 --> 00:38:43,515
- 迈克尔·甘本？你赢了他。
- 赢了！
- Michael Gambon? You've beat him.
- Yeah.

805
00:38:43,869 --> 00:38:47,484
哦太好了。既然这样，我……我倒挺想赢伊万·麦克格雷格的。
Oh that's good. In that case, I... I quite
like to beat you and McGregor.

806
00:38:47,674 --> 00:38:51,356
- 这么说吧，你的实际成绩是1分……
- 好。
- Well, you actually did it in 1 minute
- Yes.

807
00:38:51,652 --> 00:38:53,633
- 40……
- 对。
- Forty
- Yes

808
00:38:54,852 --> 00:38:57,414
- 7秒……点7！
- 漂亮！
- Seven... Point seven
- Yes

809
00:38:57,440 --> 00:39:00,076
- 哎哟不错嘛。
- 恭喜！
- Oh hello.
- Congratulations!

810
00:39:07,192 --> 00:39:08,344
你排得相当靠前啊。
You're right up there.

811
00:39:09,343 --> 00:39:11,451
事实上你仅仅落后……呃……
You're in fact only emm..

812
00:39:11,958 --> 00:39:14,608
落后那位谈吐文雅的先生0.1秒。
point one of a second behind the well spoken man.

813
00:39:14,684 --> 00:39:15,941
很好，很好。
Yes, yes.

814
00:39:15,941 --> 00:39:17,279
不管怎么说，你的位置在这儿，呃……
Anyway, so there you are, uh...

815
00:39:17,279 --> 00:39:20,222
啊等等，杰米·奥利弗是在雪地里跑的，所以他排名得往上移，对吧？
Ah sorry but Jamie Oliver was in the
snow, so he moves up, is that right?

816
00:39:20,222 --> 00:39:23,048
根本没那回事，雪早化了，他是在雪水里跑的。
No he wasn't, it had melted, he did melted snow

817
00:39:23,065 --> 00:39:25,234
- 他非说是下雪，所以我们还罚了他。
- 没错。
- He claims it was snow, and we punished him for that
- Yes

818
00:39:25,649 --> 00:39:27,318
所以不用比了，我……我觉得你比他棒，
So no, I... I think you're better

819
00:39:27,521 --> 00:39:30,552
更有趣，帅得多，而且舌头也没那么大。
and funnier and much better looking with a smaller tongue.

820
00:39:32,987 --> 00:39:34,816
女士们先生们，休·格兰特！
Ladies and gentlemen, Hugh Grant!

821
00:39:43,020 --> 00:39:48,100
好了，刚才我们测试了三款双门轿跑，来看看到底哪辆最好。
Right, now, earlier, we were testing three
coupes to decide which one is best.

822
00:39:48,100 --> 00:39:51,450
我非常、非常喜欢这辆阿尔法·罗密欧Brera。
I really really like this Alfa Romeo Brera.

823
00:39:51,450 --> 00:39:55,350
克拉克森那个蠢蛋偏偏中意这辆新款奥迪TT，
Clarkson stupidly prefers this new Audi TT

824
00:39:55,350 --> 00:39:59,750
而哈蒙德那个大傻子似乎觉得应该是这辆马自达RX-8。
and the damn fool Hammond seems to
think it should be this Mazda RX-8.

825
00:39:59,750 --> 00:40:03,270
然而到目前为止，我们什么结论也没得出来。
And so far, we have established pretty much nothing.

826
00:40:03,270 --> 00:40:04,670
但现在进入短片的第二部分，
But now in the second part of the film

827
00:40:04,670 --> 00:40:07,620
我们一路开进爱丁堡，一路接着吵。
we drive into Edinburgh and still arguing.

828
00:40:17,150 --> 00:40:20,100
你们车里的车载导航都设好了吧？
Can you set the sat nav in your car, OK?

829
00:40:20,670 --> 00:40:23,170
呃，不行，我车上压根没导航。
Err, no, I haven't got sat nav.

830
00:40:23,170 --> 00:40:24,720
你能设好吗，理查德？
Could you do that, Richard?

831
00:40:24,720 --> 00:40:27,000
我在这车里全凭直觉开。
I go by instinct in here.

832
00:40:27,650 --> 00:40:31,720
所以这要么是驾驶者之车，要么是领航员之车，
So it's the driver's car, or the navigator's car.

833
00:40:31,720 --> 00:40:34,170
要么就是空姐专车——比如你那辆，杰里米。
or the air hostess's in the case of yours Jeremy

834
00:40:34,170 --> 00:40:36,620
我觉得我大灯上落了点灰，
Think it with a bit of dust on my headlamps,

835
00:40:36,620 --> 00:40:38,550
所以顺手洗一下。
so I will just wash that off.

836
00:40:38,550 --> 00:40:40,650
搞定，我用大灯清洗装置喷干净了。
Yes, I've done that with my headlamp washers.

837
00:40:40,650 --> 00:40:42,100
你洗了吗，詹姆斯？
Have you done that, James?

838
00:40:42,100 --> 00:40:45,300
我刚才用湿手帕包着手指擦过了。
Well I did that earlier with a wet hanky and end of my finger.

839
00:40:45,300 --> 00:40:48,350
但你们俩谁有DSG双离合变速箱吗？
But either of you two got a DSG gearbox.

840
00:40:48,350 --> 00:40:49,720
- 没有。 - 没有。
- No. - No.

841
00:40:49,720 --> 00:40:52,650
你们俩谁的车有可调悬挂吗？
Have you got adjustable suspension, either of you?

842
00:40:52,650 --> 00:40:54,270
- 没有。 - 没。
- No. - No.

843
00:40:56,020 --> 00:40:58,400
但紧接着我就发射了一枚鱼雷，
But then I fired a torpedo

844
00:40:58,400 --> 00:41:01,220
直挺挺轰在“克拉克森号战列舰”的腰子上。
straight into the side of HMS Clarkson.

845
00:41:01,220 --> 00:41:05,200
杰里米，我能问问那些配置有多少是标配吗？
Jeremy, can I just ask how much of that stuff is standard.

846
00:41:05,200 --> 00:41:09,420
呃……差不多全都是选装件。
Almost everything really is an optional extra.

847
00:41:10,150 --> 00:41:12,270
那一堆选装得花多少银子？
How many is that lot cost?

848
00:41:12,270 --> 00:41:16,870
呃，这车上的选装加起来得两千镑吧。
Err, the optional extras on this car add up 2000 pounds.

849
00:41:16,870 --> 00:41:18,000
多少？！
How much?

850
00:41:18,000 --> 00:41:20,900
好吧……六千多镑。
Six (more) thousand pounds.

851
00:41:20,900 --> 00:41:22,600
六千大洋？！
Six grand?

852
00:41:22,600 --> 00:41:25,470
其实是八千，但嘘……
It's actually eight grand but shh...

853
00:41:26,950 --> 00:41:31,300
我们一路上唇枪舌剑、针锋相对，谁也不肯服软。
It was tit for tat all the way and nobody was going to give in.

854
00:41:31,670 --> 00:41:33,500
事实真相其实是这样的：
The truth of the matter is this

855
00:41:33,500 --> 00:41:34,970
你真正梦寐以求的车，
the car you really want

856
00:41:34,970 --> 00:41:36,420
得长得像阿尔法，
looks like the Alfa

857
00:41:36,420 --> 00:41:37,770
开起来像马自达，
drives like the Mazda

858
00:41:37,770 --> 00:41:39,020
造工又得像奥迪一样扎实。
and is built like the Audi.

859
00:41:39,020 --> 00:41:40,600
但既然这世上根本没这车，
But since that doesn't exist

860
00:41:40,600 --> 00:41:42,070
你就只能选奥迪。
you've got to have the Audi.

861
00:41:42,070 --> 00:41:44,850
因为它是最均衡、最完美的折中之选，
Cause it's the best all round of the best compromise

862
00:41:44,850 --> 00:41:47,370
事情就这么尘埃落定了。
and that, that's an end of it.

863
00:41:47,920 --> 00:41:51,470
但这事儿可还没完，
因为轿跑玩的就是颜值。
It wasn't the end though,
because coupes are all about looks.

864
00:41:51,470 --> 00:41:54,550
为了搞清楚我们仨的座驾谁长得最帅，
And to find out which of ours was the best looking

865
00:41:56,670 --> 00:42:01,570
我们被勒令前往爱丁堡的
苏格兰国家现代艺术馆。
we've been told to go to the Scottish National
Gallery of Modern Art in Edinburgh.

866
00:42:03,220 --> 00:42:04,850
挑战规则很简单：
The challenge was simple,

867
00:42:04,850 --> 00:42:08,650
如果这家殿堂级艺术馆要破例收藏我们其中一辆车，
if this prestigious gallery was to accept just one of our cars

868
00:42:08,650 --> 00:42:12,950
单纯论美感与艺术魅力，到底会翻谁的牌子？
based on styling and love, which would it be?

869
00:42:13,450 --> 00:42:17,070
馆方召集了一个专家评审团来定夺。
A panel of experts have been assembled to make the choice.

870
00:42:19,170 --> 00:42:20,700
而为了助推一把，
And to help things along,

871
00:42:20,700 --> 00:42:25,700
我们每人有两分钟时间，
去论证自己这辆车的艺术价值。
we'd each been given two minutes to argue
the artistic merits of our particular car.

872
00:42:26,250 --> 00:42:27,720
不过在那之前，
But before that,

873
00:42:28,200 --> 00:42:31,970
我们能在艺术馆的书店里待五分钟，临时抱佛脚恶补艺术。
five minutes in the gallery bookshop to bone up our art bit.

874
00:42:32,170 --> 00:42:33,920
有任何跟日本沾边的东西吗？
Is there anything Japanese at all?

875
00:42:33,920 --> 00:42:34,850
苏格兰艺术……
Scottish arts...

876
00:42:34,850 --> 00:42:40,520
你们有没有单本讲
阿尔法·罗密欧轿跑艺术影响力的专著？
You have like a single volume on the
artistic influence of Alfa Romeo coupes.

877
00:42:41,550 --> 00:42:45,120
呃，“日本文化总的来说……大概可比作一只生蚝。”
Err, Japanese culture in general maybe like into an oyster.

878
00:42:45,120 --> 00:42:49,550
“它敞开自身，以抗击来自……生蚝的反复冲击。”
Opening itself up to repeat the onslaughts from the... oyster.

879
00:42:52,350 --> 00:42:57,070
遗憾的是，在书店里的这通突击恶补
只让我们脑子更乱了。
Unfortunately the crash course in the bookshop
just confused us even more.

880
00:42:57,070 --> 00:43:00,770
等詹姆斯打头阵一开讲，专家们很快就领教到了。
As the experts discovered when James kicked things off.

881
00:43:01,300 --> 00:43:03,400
额，各位教授下午好。
Em, good afternoon professors.

882
00:43:03,400 --> 00:43:05,400
首先我想抛出这样一个问题：
I'd like to begin by asking the question

883
00:43:05,400 --> 00:43:07,700
汽车究竟算不算一件艺术品？
Can a car be a piece of art.

884
00:43:07,700 --> 00:43:10,150
我得当场声明，我觉得不算。
I'd like to say immediately that I think no.

885
00:43:10,150 --> 00:43:11,920
那玩意儿根本算不上艺术品，
That's not a piece of art

886
00:43:11,920 --> 00:43:16,050
但我们能否在那件设计中寻觅到艺术的痕迹？
but can we find any art in that piece of design?

887
00:43:16,050 --> 00:43:17,320
我先把这玩意儿放在这儿。
I'll put it down there.

888
00:43:17,320 --> 00:43:20,870
我真的能说奥迪TT的设计，是对维多利亚时期
Can I really argue that the Audi TT was a reaction

889
00:43:20,870 --> 00:43:24,950
那些繁复浮夸的天花板石膏顶花的反叛吗？
to the overly complicated ceiling rose of Victorian houses?

890
00:43:26,000 --> 00:43:29,450
比如，大家看这辆阿尔法·罗密欧的车灯，
For example we can see in the lights of the Alfa Romeo here

891
00:43:29,450 --> 00:43:32,200
我认为深受苏格兰色彩画派的影响，
I think the influence of the Scottish colorists,

892
00:43:32,200 --> 00:43:34,170
也就是弗格森和佩普洛两位大师。
namely Fergusson and Peploe

